WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:06.420
<i>In the beginning, God created 
the heavens and the earth.</i>

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:11.310
<i>He followed them</i>

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.980
<i>with light, waters, and the land.</i>

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:21.460
<i>Then he created the many animals 
that would inhabit it.</i>

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.880
<i>Or... that was the plan.</i>

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:26.670
<i>It got too tedious, so he outsourced it.</i>

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.180
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.130
What is that?

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.370
A-An insect!

00:02:08.710 --> 00:02:13.530
Why is that thing here?! Someone take that 
thing to the insect department, now!

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:15.020
It's coming this way!

00:02:15.020 --> 00:02:16.520
No!

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:22.530
Oh, you escaped from the insect department,
you naughty thing.

00:02:22.530 --> 00:02:27.270
Catching something that fast with her bare 
hands shows that Ueda-san really is an angel.

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.910
I can't do that.

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:31.890
Shimoda-kun, you haven't been to 
the insect department yet, right?

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:34.980
It's the door over there. 
I'll introduce you.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:36.420
O-Oh, all right.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.430
I guess the insect department 
will be full of insects.

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:41.930
<b>Insect Department</b>

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.430
Hello, everyone.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:46.550
Hey, Ueda-san.

00:02:46.550 --> 00:02:47.400
Hey, Ueda-san.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:48.410
Oh, Ueda-san!

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.060
It's Ueda-san!

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.940
It's Ueda-san!

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.250
This little dear was outside.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:56.700
We're terribly sorry that you had 
to bother yourself with this.

00:02:57.070 --> 00:03:00.380
We're in the middle of 
miniaturizing this guy.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.600
You're miniaturizing an insect?

00:03:02.600 --> 00:03:06.910
Yes, we're going to scale this 70-centimeter
 dragonfly down to one tenth of its size.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.710
I just realized they have 
huge bags under their eyes!

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:11.470
We <i>will</i> make it seven centimeters.

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:14.720
As always, your technical abilities
 are perversely good.

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:17.580
Thank you!

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:20.030
<i>Is "perverse" praise, though?</i>

00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:22.800
Now you know where
 the insect department is.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:26.880
Yes. I'm not sure if they were
unique or the exact opposite.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.290
Our company also has a rock department, 
a plant department, and—

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.040
I-I touched it! It's over...

00:03:35.040 --> 00:03:36.230
Kanamori-san?!

00:03:36.610 --> 00:03:42.110
Ah, if I have to go, I wish I could have 
died in bigger, stronger arms...

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.870
Oh, what a cute yellow frog.

00:03:43.570 --> 00:03:45.870
<b>Poison Dart Frog</b>

00:03:46.400 --> 00:03:49.820
Don't touch it! It may be small, 
but its poison is lethal!

00:03:49.820 --> 00:03:51.880
Huh? But didn't you
 just say you touched it?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:56.150
My vision's going faint. 
Please, hold my hand.

00:03:56.150 --> 00:03:57.890
Kanamori-san!

00:03:59.910 --> 00:04:00.780
But the poison...

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:06.550
It's fine. This poisonous frog accumulates 
poison by eating ants and mites.

00:04:06.550 --> 00:04:10.400
This one was just made, so it hasn't 
eaten anything. It's just a frog.

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:11.760
Phew!

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.130
I was terrified.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.900
But now that I look at it, 
it has a lovely pattern.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:18.200
Look!

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.160
See, when the eggs hatch...

00:04:22.300 --> 00:04:25.580
Oh, it puts its children on its back.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:26.690
Cute!

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:29.630
Oh, I wonder where it's going.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.290
To a small pool of water with no predators.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:37.630
If it's a small pool of water, 
won't these babies lack food?

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:38.550
They won't.

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:42.420
The eggs that the mother laid are there.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.040
<i>Cannibalism?!</i>

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:46.930
W-Wasn't there any other way?

00:04:46.930 --> 00:04:49.300
Why? Isn't it so cute?

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:51.180
C-Cute?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:55.430
God has approved that one, 
so it's already on earth.

00:04:55.430 --> 00:04:58.900
Meido-chan's specialty is 
frogs and other cute things.

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:00.370
Cute?

00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:04.360
That reminds me... A new order 
from God came in, right?

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:05.190
Ah, right.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:09.070
I believe it was for an animal 
that's "cute, but not cute."

00:05:09.350 --> 00:05:11.390
As always, so vague!

00:05:11.390 --> 00:05:13.780
I bet this'll be one we have
 to redo again and again!

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:18.170
I-It'll be fine. God trusts you guys.

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.950
The word is that "the design is up to you."

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:25.850
There has never, ever been a case where the 
client said it was up to us and <i>meant</i> it!

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:29.000
Those abstract requests 
are the absolute worst!

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:31.220
I swear, the answer is always 
"that's not quite it."

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:33.480
Don't just drop it on our lap without 
even giving it a single thought!

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.850
I'm s-sorry!

00:05:35.230 --> 00:05:36.600
I'll do it.

00:05:36.600 --> 00:05:41.620
Oh, Meido-chan's going to make 
something that's not cute? That's exciting.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:44.490
<b>A Few Days Later...</b>

00:05:43.340 --> 00:05:44.480
Hello.

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:46.770
Meido-san, how's your progress?

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.630
Good. I came up with something really cute!

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:51.820
Oh really? What's it like?

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:59.060
Well, it's a thin, long, water-loving
parasite that can take over animals' brains.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:05.520
Then the infected animal walks to the pool 
where the parasite lives, and drowns there.

00:06:05.520 --> 00:06:07.670
That'll be food for the parasite's children.

00:06:07.670 --> 00:06:09.440
<i>Th-That's not cute.</i>

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.090
Excuse me, Meido-chan? 
The idea is revolutionary,

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:16.690
but don't you think that the balance between 
cute and not-cute is a bit skewed?

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:21.050
I guess I can't just stuff 
it full of cute elements.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.730
I mean you have to consider 
the size problem, too.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:27.440
If it's supposed to infect animal brains,
 it has to be really tiny.

00:06:27.690 --> 00:06:30.710
Oh, if you need to miniaturize it, 
how about taking it to the insect department?

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.240
They might be able to give you some help.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.340
I'll go!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:35.950
<b>Insect Department</b>

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:39.710
God has spoken!

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:42.630
This is it, thanks!

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.850
Oh, sure!

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:45.220
Is that an insect?

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.220
<b>Horsehair Worm</b>

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:47.950
Accepted!

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:48.220
<b>Accepted</b>

00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:50.130
So cute!

00:06:51.890 --> 00:06:54.600
<b>Days Later</b>

00:06:52.810 --> 00:06:54.590
Hello. Uh—

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.210
What's happening in here?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.610
Meido-chan has really hit her stride.

00:07:03.750 --> 00:07:07.540
I wanted to discuss something with her, too, 
but she's been like this the entire time.

00:07:07.540 --> 00:07:09.610
Her focus is impressive.

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:12.520
Please make sure not to interrupt her.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:15.490
Yeah, when she gets like this, 
Meido always creates great stuff.

00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:21.940
One p•n•s... No, that's not it. 
It'll be cooler to have two p•n•ses.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.500
Oh, nice idea.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:28.560
Its food will be poison. It'll eat poison.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:30.940
Offspring cannibalizing 
each other is old hat.

00:07:31.560 --> 00:07:34.880
Poop! They'll grow up 
eating poop! That's it!

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.270
<b>And then...</b>

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:39.260
It's done!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:42.220
Thank you for your help, Unabara-san.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:44.260
I'm glad I was able to help.

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:46.680
Y-You finished it?

00:07:46.680 --> 00:07:48.440
Will you come to my presentation?

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:52.730
The client's order was 
"cute, but not cute."

00:07:52.730 --> 00:07:55.670
That's why I stuffed it full 
of what I find "cute."

00:07:55.670 --> 00:07:59.660
First, it eats poisonous plants. 
It doesn't eat anything else.

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:05.240
I borrowed Unabara-san's idea and added the 
same pouch function that kangaroos have.

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:09.790
But I reversed it, so the baby 
can eat their mother's poop.

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:14.420
And I made the male's p•n•s 
cool by doubling it up.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.790
Oh my, that's so cute.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.480
My understanding of "cute" is eroding.

00:08:22.560 --> 00:08:24.570
Its pupils are vertical slits.

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:26.940
It has sharp nails on its fingers.

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:29.630
And a deathly voice for intimidation.

00:08:29.630 --> 00:08:35.040
Since all of these elements are very cute, 
I made its exterior not cute at all!

00:08:36.100 --> 00:08:37.410
God has spoken!

00:08:37.720 --> 00:08:39.960
Accepted!

00:08:38.700 --> 00:08:39.910
<b>Accepted</b>

00:08:38.950 --> 00:08:40.080
<b>Koala</b>

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:42.390
See, isn't its appearance just so meh?

00:08:42.390 --> 00:08:43.450
Huh?

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:46.840
We don't quite agree, 
but I guess it fit the order.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.920
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist

00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.930
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:55.200
With its poison and little nutritional value,

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:58.440
eucalyptus is a plant that's trying 
to have no appeal as food.

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:01.420
Koalas are hardcore and eat only that.

00:09:01.630 --> 00:09:05.180
If they eat something nobody else eats,
 they have no competition.

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:09.190
In order to digest that, they have a 
lot of microbes in their gut, right?

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:12.730
Yes, the reason the children 
eat their mother's poop

00:09:12.730 --> 00:09:16.380
is to inherit the gut microbes 
that can digest the eucalyptus.

00:09:16.380 --> 00:09:18.940
Oh, right, do you want to hear 
what a koala sounds like?

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.030
That's more intense than I expected. 
How did it end up like this?

00:09:25.030 --> 00:09:28.630
Since their food has so few nutrients,
 they don't want to move.

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:31.700
So they've come to fight
 using only their voices.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:36.440
They're already exhausted just 
from digesting eucalyptus.

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:38.090
This one's really pushing it.

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:49.990
It's so elegant!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:54.850
A single long and beautiful horn, 
added to peerless functional beauty.

00:09:55.120 --> 00:10:00.630
This must be what the client wants for their 
"animal that has a cool weapon" order!

00:10:03.290 --> 00:10:04.120
<b>Rejected</b>

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:06.280
Why?

00:10:06.280 --> 00:10:07.880
Osteoporosis.

00:10:07.880 --> 00:10:11.880
So it didn't collapse due to cerebral 
anemia like the long-necked deer.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.710
It's a calcium deficiency.

00:10:13.710 --> 00:10:17.410
But I just added this 
super-cool horn to the horse!

00:10:17.410 --> 00:10:19.380
Chief Tsuchiya never gives up.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:24.240
I figured if Kimura-kun's deer is okay,
the horse would be fine, too.

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:25.140
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:25.140
<b>Elk</b>

00:10:25.330 --> 00:10:28.680
Why does only the horse 
get osteoporosis, though?

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:30.760
The elk has it, too.

00:10:30.760 --> 00:10:32.400
Really?

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:37.010
Yes, but apparently deer are fine because 
they're equipped with multiple stomachs.

00:10:37.010 --> 00:10:40.150
Tsuchiya-san's horse only 
has one stomach, so...

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:43.070
In other words, the difference
 is in nutrient absorption.

00:10:43.070 --> 00:10:44.040
I see.

00:10:44.350 --> 00:10:49.160
If you don't have a calcium reserve, 
you can't make something this extravagant.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:50.770
It's extravagant?

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:51.760
Of course.

00:10:51.750 --> 00:11:00.130
<b>Horse</b>

00:10:51.750 --> 00:11:02.760
<b>Deer</b>

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:55.840
Animal bones are like houses 
made of calcium bricks.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:59.550
Horns are made by borrowing 
bricks from the house.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:02.760
Ah, that's why the house 
itself is dilapidated.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.630
But deer can eat a ton of 
food and repair the house.

00:11:07.850 --> 00:11:11.640
A horse has a weak stomach, so it doesn't 
have the energy to repair the house.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.150
That example was kind of horrible.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:17.120
There, there...

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:20.850
I see, animals with strong 
stomachs are robust.

00:11:20.850 --> 00:11:23.290
Their poop also looks markedly different.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:25.870
Since the deer properly absorb nutrients,

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.110
their food's original shape 
cannot be discerned in their poop.

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.160
<b>Horse</b>

00:11:27.950 --> 00:11:30.160
<b>Deer</b>

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:30.170
But with horse poop, that's often possible.

00:11:30.170 --> 00:11:31.110
Want to see?

00:11:31.110 --> 00:11:32.160
I'm f-fine.

00:11:33.410 --> 00:11:36.420
Chief, if you really insist on this horn...

00:11:38.930 --> 00:11:40.730
how about sticking it on a cow?

00:11:40.730 --> 00:11:45.570
No. It's not beautiful! It's only
 beautiful because it's on a horse.

00:11:45.930 --> 00:11:48.560
Can't you do something, Higuchi-san?

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.760
When did he produce this many drafts?!

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.440
These are just different color variations!

00:11:53.690 --> 00:11:58.450
But you know, I'd like to see 
this horned horse run on earth.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.430
Mizushima-kun!

00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:05.380
How about making the horn hollow, to reduce 
the amount of calcium that's needed?

00:12:05.380 --> 00:12:07.880
Like when Kanamori was designing the birds.

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:10.200
That's it! Let's prototype that right now!

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:14.460
Beautiful!

00:12:14.540 --> 00:12:16.460
<b><i>Unicorn</i></b>

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:21.970
<b>Rejected</b>

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:23.750
It's malnutrition.

00:12:24.980 --> 00:12:29.340
Looks like it didn't have sufficient 
energy to make this huge horn.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.470
It's always lacking something.

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:33.220
It's not very efficient, huh?

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:37.030
Should we make it a cow-like horse 
with multiple stomachs?

00:12:37.930 --> 00:12:38.740
No!

00:12:40.290 --> 00:12:42.740
I know. Let's make it stupid.

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:46.230
The brain uses vast amounts of energy.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:49.190
So let's make it stupid and divert 
the excess energy to the horn.

00:12:49.190 --> 00:12:50.110
But...

00:12:50.390 --> 00:12:52.840
He's really a pursuer of beautiful design.

00:12:52.840 --> 00:12:55.850
Sometimes you need to make 
drastic decisions like that!

00:12:59.590 --> 00:13:01.260
<b><i>Unicorn</i></b>

00:13:04.130 --> 00:13:05.720
It really is beautiful!

00:13:05.720 --> 00:13:07.380
It's not collapsing this time!

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.890
It's so elegant when it walks!

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.260
It's pretty.

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:18.100
Walk back! Backwards!

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.990
Oh, no, it's pushing more.

00:13:19.990 --> 00:13:23.220
It's too dumb to know how 
to pull out its horn!

00:13:23.910 --> 00:13:25.100
Watch out!

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.230
This is no good.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.000
Wh-What if we put nerves into the horn?

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.210
If it can feel it, it'll surely 
treat the horn better!

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.760
Like teeth?

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.490
Let's add some resilience, too, 
so it doesn't break so easily!

00:13:43.490 --> 00:13:45.060
And keep it dumb?

00:13:45.510 --> 00:13:48.390
<b>Testing Island
 Galapagos</b>

00:13:57.230 --> 00:13:58.950
B-Beautiful!

00:13:58.950 --> 00:13:59.740
I agree!

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:01.530
You made so many prototypes.

00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:06.670
Watch where you're walking, you old fart.

00:14:06.670 --> 00:14:08.520
Huh? You wanna go, punk?!

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:10.020
Bring it on!

00:14:11.010 --> 00:14:13.050
They're not going to fight, are they?

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:17.400
It's fine, oversized weapons like horns 
are basically just for intimidation.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.680
Um, they're totally fighting.

00:14:30.790 --> 00:14:33.690
Those horns are too frail
 to be waved around like that.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:35.810
Another one's got its horn stuck in a tree.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:39.850
<b>Rejected</b>

00:14:39.940 --> 00:14:44.860
<b>Rejected</b>

00:14:40.600 --> 00:14:44.860
<b>Rejected</b>

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:43.390
Rejected!

00:14:43.390 --> 00:14:44.850
Th-They're all down?

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:46.360
I can't believe it.

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:51.370
D-Don't worry, Tsuchiya-san! 
They'll be accepted one day for sure!

00:14:53.780 --> 00:14:56.330
What is this horn? It's so cool.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.820
Oh, that? It's from a 
horse that got rejected.

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:02.650
May I try attaching it to an 
animal I'm making right now?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:04.130
Sure.

00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:07.890
God has spoken!

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:10.340
<b>Accepted</b>

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:11.890
<b>Narwhal</b>

00:15:08.720 --> 00:15:10.370
Accepted!

00:15:10.370 --> 00:15:11.600
Why?!

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.390
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.660
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:20.200
These antlers can weigh up to 18 kilograms.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:25.360
And they regrow every year. That must 
consume a ton of energy and calcium.

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.350
It actually leads to osteoporosis.

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:28.900
Then why do that?

00:15:28.900 --> 00:15:32.780
It's like showing off an unnecessarily 
big car that's expensive to maintain.

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.980
They're telling the females 
and their rivals that

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:38.410
they're so amazing that they can maintain 
these unnecessarily big horns.

00:15:38.660 --> 00:15:42.420
So they can avoid unnecessary fights, 
meaning their hard work pays off.

00:15:42.660 --> 00:15:45.600
What about this horn, though?

00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:48.930
It looks like a horn, 
but it's a really long tooth.

00:15:48.930 --> 00:15:51.490
It's got nerve endings and can 
even sense the temperature.

00:15:51.490 --> 00:15:54.420
So it's not just a meaningless decoration.

00:15:57.260 --> 00:15:58.570
Hello—

00:16:00.940 --> 00:16:03.290
What's happening? Why are 
you all dressed like this?

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.580
Oh just in time, Shimoda-kun.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:09.450
We're all going to Galapagos. 
Hurry up and change!

00:16:09.450 --> 00:16:13.070
Unabara-san came up with 
some new marine animals.

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:14.810
Let's fire it up!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Pacific
White-Sided
 Dolphin</b>

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Burmeister's
 Porpoise</b>

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Beaked
Whale</b>

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:18.490 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Common
Bottlenose
Dolphin</b>

00:16:18.740 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Pilot Whale</b>

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.330
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:21.340
Accepted!

00:16:21.340 --> 00:16:24.140
Wow, it's an acceptance jackpot!

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:29.700
The client really likes these animals, 
so all sorts of these designs passed.

00:16:29.910 --> 00:16:32.310
So we were all working on these together.

00:16:32.310 --> 00:16:34.840
But why is there a mix 
of dolphins and whales?

00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:38.100
They're just different in size.
Otherwise, dolphins and whales are the same.

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:39.720
<b>Striped
Dolphin</b>

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:40.110
Accepted!

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:39.640
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:41.310
<b>Spectacled
Porpoise</b>

00:16:40.110 --> 00:16:41.640
Accepted!

00:16:40.680 --> 00:16:41.310
<b>Accepted</b>

00:16:41.220 --> 00:16:43.310
<b>Kelpie</b>

00:16:41.640 --> 00:16:43.130
Rejected!

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.310
<b>Rejected</b>

00:16:43.130 --> 00:16:46.090
Oh, no! I worked so hard on that kelpie!

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:48.280
What made you think that would work?

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:50.240
I thought that it could maybe 
slip by with the others.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:53.800
The base for the dolphin 
wasn't the horse, either.

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.470
Oh, then what was it?

00:16:55.470 --> 00:16:56.510
You want to know?

00:16:56.510 --> 00:16:57.600
Okay, quiz time!

00:16:57.280 --> 00:17:03.250
<b>Migratory Bird</b>

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:03.250
<b>Seal</b>

00:16:57.600 --> 00:16:59.610
Which baby here is the base?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:03.250
<b>Hippopotamus</b>

00:16:59.610 --> 00:17:00.960
A: Seal.

00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.120
B: Migratory bird.

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:03.250
C: Hippopotamus.

00:17:03.250 --> 00:17:05.750
Maybe the seal?

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:10.130
Too bad! The answer was C, the hippopotamus!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:11.110
Really?

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:13.060
It looks quite different, though.

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:17.240
I see. The eyes would be injured if they 
are in the front when swimming fast,

00:17:17.240 --> 00:17:18.500
so you moved them to the side?

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:21.510
Right, and because it's cuter this way.

00:17:22.200 --> 00:17:24.390
And the nose went this way.

00:17:25.210 --> 00:17:28.640
So the sea water doesn't flow in?
That's groundbreaking.

00:17:28.640 --> 00:17:31.360
Yes, and because it's cuter this way.

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:32.530
And I took off the ears, too.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:37.340
Hippos can sleep on land, but dolphins
 are always under water, right?

00:17:37.340 --> 00:17:38.530
Won't they sink?

00:17:38.530 --> 00:17:40.880
That's why the brain was tweaked.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.570
We made the left and right
hemispheres of its brain independent,

00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:45.540
so they can take turns sleeping.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.720
So that's why they can 
sleep without drowning.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.750
<b>Monkeys
</b>and
such

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.750
<b>Left Hemisphere</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.750
<b>Right Hemisphere</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.790
<b>Corpus Callosum</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:51.550
<b>Optical Nerve</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:51.550
<b>Left Hemisphere</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:51.550
<b>Right Hemisphere</b>

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:51.550
<b>Dolphins
</b> are like this

00:17:47.720 --> 00:17:51.550
Ah, so one half of the 
brain is always awake!

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:54.330
By the way, what do they eat?

00:17:54.330 --> 00:17:56.790
Uh, well, squid and such.

00:17:57.030 --> 00:18:00.640
So it eats these cute babies I created.

00:18:01.060 --> 00:18:04.080
Meido-san, aren't you 
holding it upside down?

00:18:04.080 --> 00:18:05.550
This is the top.

00:18:05.550 --> 00:18:08.690
After the tentacles, there's the head,
 then the body.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:06.810
<b>Head</b>

00:18:07.060 --> 00:18:08.690
<b>Head</b>

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:07.810
<b>Body</b>

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:08.690
<b>Body</b>

00:18:09.000 --> 00:18:11.840
Incidentally, it poops from 
the side of its head.

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:16.080
Meido-chan's imagination is really powerful.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:20.330
But since Unabara-san's dolphins are smart,
 my babies get eaten a lot.

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.460
I've decided! I'll make them talk, too!
 I'll make them smart!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:27.370
You want to equip them 
with vocal organs now?

00:18:27.370 --> 00:18:32.400
What about changing body color, 
something like flag signaling?

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:33.470
Would that be understood, though?

00:18:33.690 --> 00:18:36.710
Quiz! What is the meaning of this pattern?

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:39.540
I think the testicles are there, so maybe...

00:18:39.540 --> 00:18:42.400
"I'm incredibly virile!"

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:45.580
It worked! Kin-chan, you're amazing!

00:18:45.580 --> 00:18:48.740
And they show off something larger 
than their actual testicles.

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:50.800
I guess even squid are vain.

00:18:50.800 --> 00:18:53.860
That's amazing. Meido-chan can't be beat.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.430
They won't lose to dolphins!

00:18:56.850 --> 00:18:59.780
Squids have three hearts, 
giving them more mobility!

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.730
This way, they can escape into deep water,
 where no light penetrates!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:06.750
Huh, but... then, um... who cares
 that it's deep water?

00:19:06.980 --> 00:19:10.250
The dolphins will use echolocation to find 
squid without needing light!

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:11.890
Is this a fight?

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:14.370
Oh, looks like this will be fun.

00:19:15.840 --> 00:19:17.480
Animal battle!

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:18.890
Survival of the fittest!

00:19:18.890 --> 00:19:21.370
The dolphin is going straight for the squid!

00:19:21.370 --> 00:19:23.380
But what is echolocation, anyway?

00:19:23.600 --> 00:19:28.000
Simply put, it's sensing distance and 
direction using reflected sound waves.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.010
Smoke screen!

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.270
Are you sure squid ink will 
do anything in the darkness?

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:37.280
Then I'll evolve the smoke screen!
A smoke screen of light!

00:19:39.090 --> 00:19:41.030
<i>It's like there are no rules anymore.</i>

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:43.100
And the squid itself will shine, too!

00:19:43.100 --> 00:19:44.410
You're losing your touch, Meido-chan!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.910
In the ocean, the shinier you are,
 the more visible you are!

00:19:46.910 --> 00:19:48.330
You're the one losing your touch!

00:19:48.330 --> 00:19:51.660
Rise up near the surface! 
With the sun as the backdrop!

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:53.160
Wh-What the—?!

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.870
The squid disappeared in the sunlight!?

00:19:56.590 --> 00:19:59.660
But we still have the 
echolocation on our side!

00:19:59.930 --> 00:20:01.140
Advance!

00:20:02.030 --> 00:20:06.150
Hidden Technique: Surface Escape Mega Jump!

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.560
<b>Flying Squid</b>

00:20:06.150 --> 00:20:07.540
It flew!

00:20:07.540 --> 00:20:10.030
Oh, so those fin-like things were wings.

00:20:10.030 --> 00:20:12.220
It's jumping by ejecting sea water!

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:13.000
Good job!

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.320
Both of you, keep going!

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:16.430
That's nothing! The dolphin will jump, too!

00:20:18.370 --> 00:20:20.440
Then I'll use my last resort!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:23.340
Giant squid upgrade!

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:25.830
I'll match you on that!

00:20:29.330 --> 00:20:30.570
God has spoken!

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.990
Accepted!

00:20:32.080 --> 00:20:34.040
<b>Accepted</b>

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:34.040
<b>Giant
 Squid</b>

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:36.880
No way, the big squid passed!

00:20:36.880 --> 00:20:39.420
Aha, the client's watching the battle, too.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:47.080
Meido-chan, you made me go all-out.
 It was a good battle.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.510
But it's time to end this.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:57.770
Echolocation update! Ultrasonic beam!

00:20:58.180 --> 00:21:00.370
Accepted!

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:02.360
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:00.030 --> 00:21:02.360
<b>Sperm
 Whale</b>

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:09.840
No way! I can't believe your beam got accepted!

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.840
Next time, I won't lose!

00:21:13.870 --> 00:21:18.380
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:18.060
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:18.560 --> 00:21:20.540
Total length: 18 meters!

00:21:20.540 --> 00:21:22.520
That's about as long as a train car.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:26.790
Can such a large animal really 
emit a beam from its head?

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:27.850
It can.

00:21:27.850 --> 00:21:34.570
What's more, it can direct sound so 
intense that it makes its prey faint.

00:21:34.570 --> 00:21:36.530
I can't quite imagine how.

00:21:36.530 --> 00:21:41.270
A sperm whale can output 
a maximum of 250 decibels.

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:46.740
For reference, a jet engine is about 
120 decibels if you're standing next to it.

00:21:46.740 --> 00:21:51.080
Wow. The sperm whale must be 
fighting really formidable foes!

00:21:51.080 --> 00:21:53.770
That's why it evolved to get 
so big to deal with them!

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:58.040
Sperm whales often have scars on 
their heads that are assumed to be

00:21:58.040 --> 00:21:59.660
from battles with giant squid.

00:21:59.660 --> 00:22:03.540
So the ruthless battle between 
these two is never going to end!

00:22:04.750 --> 00:22:06.050
God has spoken!

00:22:06.270 --> 00:22:08.120
Accepted!

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:09.050
<b>Accepted</b>

00:22:07.840 --> 00:22:09.050
<b>Sea Horse</b>

00:22:09.050 --> 00:22:13.100
Yay! When I made that kelpie from 
earlier smaller, it passed!

00:22:13.100 --> 00:22:14.720
Congratulations.

